notes: This source-qualified commercial complex nutrient is BD-Difco TC Yeastolate
  before the separate recipe processing steps. JCM896 explicitly names TC Yeastolate
  (BD-Difco) as a weighed ingredient; its catalogue and lot are unstated. The two
  TOGO2179/2578-derived recipe occurrences explicitly identify BD255772 in 10% and
  2% preparations. The primary paper Characterization of yeastolate fractions that
  promote insect cell growth and recombinant protein production (PMC2267510), methods
  section Yeastolate and preparation of yeastolate fractions, independently identifies
  Difco TC yeastolate catalogue255772 purchased from Becton Dickinson, then describes
  dissolving and ultrafiltering it. The latter ultrafiltration and ethanol fractions
  are subsequent preparations and are not intrinsic properties assigned to the product
  here. The common TC product name and manufacturer support this bounded product-family
  identity; a particular catalogue or lot is not retroactively assigned to JCM896.
  Raw labels TC Yeastolate (BD-Difco) and TC Yeastolate (BD 255772) are retained as
  occurrence provenance without global synonym approval. Do not merge this product
  with generic yeast extract, historical Proteose Yeastolate Difco5577-15, the MICRO0000522
  2%-autoclaved stock, or whole 2%/10% solutions. No composition, lot invariance,
  catalogue-successor equivalence or individual nutrient role is asserted.
